WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.706
A Witness-style line

00:00:01.517 --> 00:00:02.708
puzzle game running

00:00:03.246 --> 00:00:04.496
Steren built Circle

00:00:04.307 --> 00:00:05.097
with a Line

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.441
a standalone puzzle

00:00:06.253 --> 00:00:07.491
game for Waveshare's

00:00:07.303 --> 00:00:11.158
1.8-inch ESP32-S3 AMOLED

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:11.736
touch board

00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:12.915
in plain C

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:14.165
on ESP-IDF with

00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:15.227
procedural puzzles

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.630
and synthesized audio

00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:18.101
The homage to

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:18.950
The Witness boots

00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:19.528
straight into the

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:19.870
game

00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:20.931
and generates its

00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:22.558
panel puzzles procedurally

00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:24.068
with vector graphics

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.377
and audio created

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:26.167
from scratch

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:27.963
The board-support layer

00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:28.836
handles display

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:29.579
touch

00:00:29.685 --> 00:00:30.852
buttons and audio

00:00:30.782 --> 00:00:31.619
and detects the

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.975
newer V2 hardware

00:00:32.787 --> 00:00:33.706
revision at boot

00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:34.555
by probing the

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.558
touch controller's

00:00:35.381 --> 00:00:36.607
I2C address

00:00:37.134 --> 00:00:38.148
Full story on

00:00:37.959 --> 00:00:38.855
the dashboard
